Audio through ALSA: OH's audio HDI in its ALSA mode (drivers_peripheral_audio_feature_alsa_lib) with the board's
hooks (device/board/oneplus 0005), alsa-lib with its configuration files (alsa_lib_feature_config_enable: without
it alsa-lib loads no configuration and cannot open "hw:0"), and alsa_adapter.json naming the OnePlus 6's card
(ALSA id O6, card 0) as the primary adapter. The port's files were the rk3568 templates (card rockchiprk809co,
ADM mode), so OH had no working audio at all.

audio_policy_config.xml: OH 7.0's policy reads the version 2.0 format (adapters, pipes, devices); the port's file
was the 1.0 format (deviceclass/modules), so the policy never opened the primary output ("adapter primary is
nullptr", "can not find sink Speaker"). This is the rk3568 7.0 file with the primary pipes at 48 kHz.

alsa-lib's configuration on the vendor side: libasound reads /vendor/etc/audio/alsa/share (ALSA_CONFIG_DIR in
third_party/alsa-lib include/config.h), but alsa-lib's own prebuilt targets install alsa.conf and the rest into the
system image (/system/etc/audio/alsa/share), so with alsa_lib_feature_config_enable alone it still found no
configuration. The product installs alsa.conf and smixer.conf where libasound looks.

